alex: Heads-up, opened docs PR to refresh streaming + pagination snippets across py/ts/go. Trying to make them minimal and copy-paste friendly. PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/4912
jia: Skimming now. Primary checks: simple backoff pattern, explicit abort/cancel handling, and an example that shows pagination cursor use with streaming (so people don't mix up cursor vs offset).

tmiller: Note: runtime changed the retry config key last sprint. New shape is `retries.max_attempts` in JS/Py configs. We should include both old and new shapes for a short window.

alex: Good call. I'll add both, with a comment on runtime >=2.1 for the new shape.

sam: Re: Go  the Go client still uses the old field `MaxRetries` in options. I'd prefer we show a conditional comment rather than two full Go snippets. Also: show signal-aware context to avoid leaking goroutines on Ctrl+C.

alex: Agreed. Draft TS snippet below, planning to put in docs/examples/streaming.md. Thoughts?
```
// ts: stream-example.ts
const ac = new AbortController();
setTimeout(() => ac.abort(), 30_000);
try {
  for await (const part of client.stream({ model: 'rw/fast-13b', retries: { max_attempts: 3 }, signal: ac.signal })) {
    process.stdout.write(part.text);
  }
} catch (err) {
  console.error('stream error', err);
}
```

jia: Looks good. Add a one-liner about partial results ordering (they are emitted monotonic for a single request). Also link to the small test in examples/test_stream_order.py.

alex: I'll add a tiny pytest that asserts sequence IDs. I'll paste the python test idea:
```
# examples/test_stream_order.py
def test_chunk_order(client):
    ids = []
    for chunk in client.stream({ 'model': 'rw/fast-13b' }):
        ids.append(chunk.seq)
    assert ids == sorted(ids)
```

sam: For Go, propose this pattern (compact) to show both signal handling and a basic retry loop. Less verboseness so readers copy it inline:
```
// stream_retry.go
ctx, stop := signal.NotifyContext(context.Background(), os.Interrupt)
defer stop()
opts := StreamOptions{Model: "rw/fast-13b", MaxRetries: 3} // for runtime <2.1
for attempt := 0; attempt < 5; attempt++ {
    err := runStream(ctx, opts)
    if err == nil || ctx.Err() != nil { break }
    time.Sleep(time.Duration(math.Pow(2, float64(attempt))) * 150 * time.Millisecond)
}
```

jia: Include a comment pointing to the backoff-jitter doc (eng-runtime/backoff.md) and mention using full jitter for production.

tmiller: I'll add a short blurb to the migration guide calling out the rename and linking to the PR in runtime. Also, confirm the canonical example uses `retries.max_attempts` in the new docs.

